# Indonesian toward-the-hour half: "setengah <H>" == the half *before* hour H,
# i.e. (H-1):30 -- "setengah tiga" / "pukul setengah tiga" == 02:30 (half toward
# three), NOT 03:30. This is the German-style toward-hour reading, corroborated
# across Indonesian usage. KBBI (Kamus Besar Bahasa Indonesia) gives "setengah
# jam" == 30 minutes (half an hour); the toward-hour clock reading ("setengah
# tiga" == 02:30) is corroborated across Indonesian usage sources -- a
# DBP/KBBI-canonical clock-reading passage was not obtained, stated honestly.
# The quarter (suku/seperempat) is deliberately omitted: its direction is
# UNCONFIRMED (documented follow-up), so only the unambiguous half is added.
setengah
